    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## soc-triage \u2014 Alert Triage & IOC Enrichment\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n**TRIGGER**   Schedule every 30s\n**OUTPUT**    Discord/Slack alert card per alert + Supabase status update\n**DEPENDS ON** soc-ingest (inserts alerts) \u00b7 Supabase alert_queue \u00b7 VirusTotal \u00b7 AbuseIPDB \u00b7 MalwareBazaar\n**AUTHOR**    S2K7x  \u00b7  **UPDATED** 2026-05\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n**PIPELINE**\n`Supabase (pending)` \u2192 `Check Queue` \u2192 `SplitInBatches Per Alert` \u2192 `Init Context` \u2192 `IF Has IOCs?`\n  \u251c\u2500 No IOC  \u2192 `Build No-IOC Message` \u2192 `Discord` \u2192 `Mark Done`\n  \u2514\u2500 Has IOC \u2192 `SplitInBatches Per IOC` \u2192 `VT + AbuseIPDB / MalwareBazaar` \u2192 `Build Slack` \u2192 `Slack` \u2192 `Mark Done`\n",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 4220,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "99a5a4a5-9f2b-4edb-9e7f-8793260f81bf",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 \u2014 Intake & Cleanup\nRuns every 30 seconds:\n1. **Stuck Job Cleanup** \u2192 reset alerts stuck in `status='processing'` for more than 5 min back to `pending`\n2. **Fetch Pending Alerts** \u2192 SELECT * WHERE status = 'pending' ORDER BY created_at ASC\n3. **Check Queue** \u2192 filters items without `id`, caps at **5 alerts/cycle**, sets `_queue_saturated` flag if > 50 pending\n",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 890,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "612fb501-9927-4d7b-9511-4da039cfbc0c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 \u2014 Queue Routing\n**IF Queue Saturated?** \u2192 if `_queue_saturated` flag is set\n  \u2192 `true`: send Slack team notification\n\n**SplitInBatches \u2014 Per Alert**\nProcesses **one alert at a time** via loop-back.\n\u26a0\ufe0f Loop-back can carry Supabase response rows or\n   error-bubbles \u2014 both are filtered by the guard\n   in Section 3.\n",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "916ace93-51cf-4657-9260-bff87c51b3dc",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -280,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 \u2014 Alert Context  \u26a0\ufe0f (read this)\n\n**Code \u2014 Init Alert Context** is the central guard of the workflow.\n\n### Infinite-loop guard\n```\nif (item.error)                    return [];  // error-bubble from Continue on Fail\nif (item._queue_saturated)         return [];  // sentinel from Check Queue\nif (!alertId || !item.rule_id\n    || item.status !== 'pending')  return [];  // Supabase Mark Done loop-back\n```\nWithout this guard \u2192 `Supabase Mark Done` returns the updated row\n(status='done') back into SplitInBatches \u2192 treated as a new alert\n\u2192 **infinite loop of 60+ iterations**.\n\n### sd.currentAlert pattern\nThe alert is stored in `$getWorkflowStaticData('global').currentAlert`.\nAll downstream Code nodes read from `sd.currentAlert`, **not** from\n`$input.first().json` \u2014 because Supabase Mark Processing returns a raw\nNode.js HTTP stream, not the alert data.\n",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "154fa8d1-3dbe-4dc6-b33f-6c803b4eddca",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 \u2014 No-IOC Path\nThe alert has no IOCs to enrich.\n\u2192 **Code \u2014 Build No-IOC Message** reads alert from `sd.currentAlert`\n\u2192 Formats with severity prefix `[LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / CRITICAL]` based on `rule_level`\n\u2192 **Discord**: sends formatted alert card\n\u2192 **Supabase**: sets `status = 'done'`\n",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "ae635b86-ddd8-45d8-9ea3-a49619e133f7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 \u2014 IOC Enrichment Loop\n**SplitInBatches \u2014 Per IOC** processes each IOC one at a time (IP / hash / domain).\n",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 1560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "03e782b8-1cca-4b4a-a8dd-59b1cb932bbe",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        450
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**VT Rate Limit Guard** \u2192 enforces a 15-second pause between VirusTotal calls (free tier: 4 req/min).\nThe current IOC is saved in `sd.currentIoc` so Format nodes can reference it.\n\n**Routing by IOC type:**\n`ip`     \u2192 VirusTotal IP + AbuseIPDB    \u2192 `Format IP Result`    (MALICIOUS if vt > 5 OR abuse > 50%)\n`hash`   \u2192 VirusTotal Hash + MalwareBazaar \u2192 `Format Hash Result`  (MALICIOUS if vt > 5 OR found in MB)\n`domain` \u2192 VirusTotal Domain             \u2192 `Format Domain Result` (MALICIOUS if vt > 5)\n\n**Possible verdicts:** `CLEAN` \u00b7 `SUSPICIOUS` \u00b7 `MALICIOUS` \u00b7 `UNKNOWN` (when API returns an error)\nResults accumulate in `sd.enrichedIocs[]` via `$getWorkflowStaticData('global')`.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Format nodes read responses via `$items('HTTP \u2014 VT IP')` etc. \u2014 they do **not** rely on `$input`.\n   They detect `vt.error` and return `UNKNOWN` verdict instead of a false `CLEAN`.\n",
        "height": 550,
        "width": 1550,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "098fda96-8647-4806-a219-8628376801c5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        510
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6 \u2014 Final Output (with IOCs)\n**Code \u2014 Build Slack Message**:\n- Reads `sd.currentAlert` + `sd.enrichedIocs`\n- Clears `sd` after use to avoid stale data in the next cycle\n- Bail-out if `alert.id` is missing \u2192 returns `{ _skipped: true }`\n\n\u2192 **Slack**: enriched alert card with all IOC verdicts\n\u2192 **Supabase**: sets `status = 'done'`\n",
        "height": 230,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "fb7419a9-7e19-445a-a9d1-588157f3dcdd",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2360,
        450
      ]
    }
